  "solution": {
    "brief": "Wasp example 29: constraints series continued",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: wasp_30 directly continues this constraints series, extending the constraint techniques with orientation-based constraints. wasp_29 is thus the immediate prerequisite for wasp_30 in the constraints sub-series.\n\nRelated insight: wasp_33 further continues this constraints series beyond wasp_30, confirming the constraints sub-series extends through at least tutorial 33. Tutorial 33 adds export, DisCo, and connection-rules as techniques that emerge later in the constraints series, indicating the series progressively incorporates more advanced export and rule-based connection configuration workflows.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The stochastic, connection-rules, and multiple-part-types techniques in wasp_29 are directly complemented by smart-attribute workflows (as in wasp_stochastic_aggregation_smart_attributes), where attributes on parts drive which connection rules are evaluated during stochastic aggregation. Mesh-based part geometry and custom-preview are practical extensions of the brep-geometry approach used in this tutorial.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The stochastic, rule-based, multiple-part-types techniques in wasp_29 are directly extended by advanced aggregation workflows (such as wasp_stochastic_aggregation_hierarchy) that add explicit part hierarchy retrieval and structured rule generation on top of constraint-based stochastic assembly — providing a hierarchical organizational layer to the part and connection infrastructure established here.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: The advanced stochastic aggregation hierarchy workflow (wasp_stochastic_aggregation_hierarchy) builds directly on the rule-based, multiple-part-types, and connection-configuration foundations in wasp_29, and further demonstrates that custom-preview and orientation-aware connection configurations are natural extensions of the constraint and attribute-driven techniques established here.",
